{{- /*
sales.gohtml is the sales report: the lines sold in a period, newest sale first.

The rows come from the cross-module read layer, not from a module's service: the
panel knows no module (ADR 0011). Two reads stand behind one row — the line
(what sold, how many, for how much) and its order (when, under which number, in
which currency) — and they are joined in Go rather than here, so a row whose
order could not be found is still printed instead of half-rendered.

Every field is printed as an ordinary value, so the template engine's escaping
applies to all of them. A line's title is the copy of a product name taken at
the moment of sale, which means it is text somebody typed, and this panel runs
inside an administrator's session.

THE PERIOD IS INCLUSIVE ON SCREEN AND HALF-OPEN IN THE QUERY. The "to" box holds
the last day the report covers; the filter behind it stops at the start of the
day after that, so a report for 1-31 August contains everything placed on the
31st. The form and the paging links carry both dates, because a "next" that
dropped them would quietly move the reader to the last thirty days.

THERE IS NO TOTAL, and its absence is deliberate. Only one page of at most 25
rows is ever in hand — the read layer offers no aggregation and clamps the
limit — so a sum printed here would be the takings of these 25 lines while
reading as the takings of the period. A wrong number nobody can see is worse
than a missing one: a missing total sends someone to write the query.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>{{ .Title }}</h1>

<form method="get" action="{{ .Path }}">
  <label for="from">From (inclusive)</label>
  <input id="from" type="date" name="from" value="{{ .From }}">
  <label for="to">To (inclusive)</label>
  <input id="to" type="date" name="to" value="{{ .To }}">
  <p><button type="submit">Show period</button></p>
</form>

<p class="muted">Sold lines placed from {{ .From }} to {{ .To }}, both days included.</p>

{{ if .Sales }}
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Placed</th><th>Order</th><th>Sold as</th><th>Variant</th>
      <th class="num">Quantity</th><th class="num">Unit price</th><th class="num">Total</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {{ range .Sales }}
    <tr>
      {{- /*
      The day is the ORDER's, not the line's: a line added to an existing order
      carries the day of the exchange, and dating an exchange as a fresh sale
      would move trade between two reporting periods.
      */ -}}
      <td>
        {{ if not .PlacedAt.IsZero }}{{ .PlacedAt.Format "2006-01-02" }}
        {{ else }}<span class="muted">unknown</span>{{ end }}
      </td>
      <td>
        {{ if .DisplayID }}<a href="{{ $.OrdersPath }}/{{ .OrderID }}">#{{ .DisplayID }}</a>
        {{ else }}<span class="muted">no order</span>{{ end }}
      </td>
      {{- /*
      The title is the name the line was SOLD UNDER, copied at the moment of
      sale. It is not the variant's current name on purpose: a catalog rename
      must not rewrite what a past sale says it was.
      */ -}}
      <td>{{ if .Title }}{{ .Title }}{{ else }}<span class="muted">untitled</span>{{ end }}</td>
      {{- /*
      The variant identifier is shown next to it because that is what an
      operator pastes into a catalog search; the historical title may no longer
      find anything.
      */ -}}
      <td>{{ if .VariantID }}{{ .VariantID }}{{ else }}<span class="muted">none</span>{{ end }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ .Quantity }}</td>
      {{- /*
      An amount whose currency scale could not be read is shown as minor units
      and SAID to be, rather than being divided by a guessed hundred: that would
      print the wrong figure for every 0-digit and 3-digit currency. A line
      whose order was not found has no currency at all, which is the same state.
      */ -}}
      <td class="num">{{ .UnitPrice }} {{ .Currency }}</td>
      <td class="num">
        {{ .Total }} {{ .Currency }}{{ if .Minor }} <span class="muted">(minor)</span>{{ end }}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {{ end }}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{ else }}
<p class="muted">No sold lines in this period.</p>
{{ end }}

<nav>
  {{ if .HasPrev }}
  <a href="{{ .Path }}?page={{ .PrevPage }}&amp;from={{ .From }}&amp;to={{ .To }}">Previous</a>
  {{ end }}
  <span class="muted">Page {{ .Page }}</span>
  {{ if .HasNext }}
  <a href="{{ .Path }}?page={{ .NextPage }}&amp;from={{ .From }}&amp;to={{ .To }}">Next</a>
  {{ end }}
</nav>
{{ end }}
